─── app/api/scene_manual_revision.py:23-26 ───
[other · medium] These two handlers are `async def` but they call the service (`revise_scene_labels`
/ `withdraw_slice`), which does blocking synchronous ORM I/O on a sync `Session` (several `select`
queries, inserts, `db.commit()`). In FastAPI an `async def` route runs on the event loop, so this
stalls the whole loop for every DB round-trip, contradicting the documented repo convention (see
`app/api/ingest_submissions.py`: read the body in an async dependency, then use a sync `def` route
so ORM runs in the threadpool; `app/api/pipelines.py` uses sync `def` + Pydantic body). Applies to
both `revise_scene_labels` and `withdraw_slice` below.

Additionally, `await request.json()` is unguarded: an empty body, invalid JSON, or
valid-JSON-but-non-dict payload (`[]`, `"x"`) raises `json.JSONDecodeError`/`AttributeError` on the
later `.get(...)` calls → 500 instead of 422, unlike the rest of the API.

Suggested fix: buffer/parse the body in an async dependency that maps parse errors to 422, and make
the handlers sync `def`.

