─── app/api/scene_manual_revision.py:26-29 ───
[other · medium] The body is read with raw `await request.json()` instead of a FastAPI/pydantic
model, so the error surface is inconsistent and partly unhandled: malformed JSON → 400 from
Starlette, but a missing body → `ClientDisconnect` (a BaseException, not an HTTPException) → 500,
and a JSON body that is not an object (e.g. a list or scalar) passes `request.json()` fine, then
crashes with `AttributeError` inside `idempotency_key(payload.get(...))` / the service's
`body.get(...)` → 500. Sibling API modules in this repo parse bodies through a pydantic DTO and
explicitly map validation failures to 422 (see `ingest_submissions._parse_model`). Suggest a
pydantic request model (with `extra="forbid"` / type constraints for `row_version`, `reason`,
`scene_code`, `idempotency_key`, `corrected_label`, `operator`), or at minimum `data = await
request.json()` followed by `if not isinstance(data, dict): raise HTTPException(422, ...)`. Note the
handler docstrings already document the body contract as a JSON object, so rejecting non-object
payloads keeps behavior consistent with the documented API.


